Description: Implements permutation-based inference for conditional logistic
    regression fitted to matched case-control data, where several units share
    an event (a matched set) and only some of them act. Rather than relying on
    the asymptotic standard errors reported by 'survival::clogit()', which can
    be unreliable with many small strata or rare outcomes, the outcome is
    repeatedly shuffled within matched sets and the model refitted to build an
    empirical null distribution for each coefficient. Zero p-values are
    replaced by a pseudo-count following Knijnenburg et al. (2009)
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btp211>. The package also provides simulators
    for matched case-control event data and a helper for computing running
    exposure covariates from a longitudinal event log. The approach follows
    Ridgeway (2016) <doi:10.1080/2330443X.2015.1129918>.
